{title: Oh Susanna}
{composer: Stephen Foster}
{key: C}
{genre: Folk}
{language: English}

{section: Verse 1}
I [C]come from Alabama with my [G]banjo on my [C]knee
I'm [C]going to Louisiana my [G]true love for to [C]see
It [C]rained all night the day I left the [G]weather it was [C]dry
The [C]sun so hot I froze to death [G]Susanna don't you [C]cry

{section: Chorus}
[F]Oh Susanna oh [C]don't you cry for [G]me
For I [C]come from Alabama with my [G]banjo on my [C]knee

{section: Verse 2}
I [C]had a dream the other night when [G]everything was [C]still
I [C]dreamed I saw Susanna a [G]coming down the [C]hill
The [C]buckwheat cake was in her mouth the [G]tear was in her [C]eye
Says [C]I'm coming from the south [G]Susanna don't you [C]cry

{section: Chorus}
